### Commit `3c08882` — Deck view text overlap fix
**Files:** `frontend/src/pages/DeckViewPG.tsx`, `frontend/src/pages/DeckView.tsx` (two-line change total)

Root cause: `QueuePositionDisplay` and `VerbCycler` were both gated on `isGenerating` alone, so both rendered simultaneously during the queue-wait state — producing the jumbled text overlap observed on both skins (more severe on Glassy due to `space-y-2` tight spacing).

Fix: made them mutually exclusive by tightening the `VerbCycler` render condition.

```diff
- <VerbCycler intervalMs={5000} />
+ {hasChecked && !shouldShowQueue && <VerbCycler intervalMs={5000} />}
```

State matrix verified:
- Queue wait (pending/approved): QPD visible, VerbCycler hidden
- Active processing: QPD hidden, VerbCycler + ParticleSpinner + progress bar visible
- Not generating: neither visible
- Before first poll (`!hasChecked`): QPD visible ("Checking…"), VerbCycler hidden

Not touched: `QueuePositionDisplay.tsx`, `VerbCycler.tsx`, `spinnerVerbs.ts`, `useQueuePosition.ts`, `GeneratePG.tsx`, `GenerateGO.tsx`, translations. Post-submit "Forging Memories" orb on Generate pages confirmed unaffected.

### Commit `eefa26e` — Enrichment article-strip + German noun capitalization
**Files:** `orchestrator/src/services/enrichment.py`, `orchestrator/tests/test_enrichment.py` (+481 / −2)

Two-layer fix for the `"der parrot"` translation corruption bug:

**Layer A — prompt tightening:**
- `translation` bullet now reads: `"the bare translated word or phrase in {base_language} only, with no leading articles, no part-of-speech markers, and no quotation marks"`
- `word_target` bullet now pins target-language orthography: German nouns capitalized, Romance-language nouns lowercase unless proper nouns
- Word `determiners` deliberately dropped after pass-1 review flagged it as over-broad (would cause LLM to strip meaningful demonstratives like `this`/`that`)

**Layer B — post-processing helpers with base-language collision guard:**

- `_TARGET_LANGUAGE_ARTICLES` constant covering `de/fr/it/es/pt/nl/en` — definite + indefinite + Romance contractions (`l'`, `un'`, `d'`)
- `_BASE_LANGUAGE_PROTECTED_TOKENS` constant covering same set of ISO codes — protects base-language articles, pronouns, and common function words from being accidentally stripped when they collide with a target-language article
- `_strip_target_article(translation, target_lang_code, base_lang_code)` — only strips when head token is in target article set AND NOT in base protected set
- `_capitalize_german_noun(word_target, target_lang_code, pos)` — fires only when target is `de` and pos is `noun`
- Both helpers wired into `run_enrichment` after JSON parse, before return
- Defensive: None, non-string, empty, whitespace-only, apostrophe-contracted edge cases all guarded; never returns empty string for non-empty input

**Critical homograph collisions that the base-protection set fixes** (each would have permanently corrupted translations in Supabase if shipped without the guard):
- Target=it, base=en: `"I go"` stayed `"I go"` (Italian `i` article would have stripped English pronoun `I`)
- Target=de, base=en: `"die alone"` stayed `"die alone"` (German `die` article would have stripped English verb `die`)
- Target=pt, base=en: `"a house"` stayed `"a house"` (Portuguese `a` article would have stripped English `a`)
- Target=pt, base=en: `"as if"` stayed `"as if"` (Portuguese `as` would have stripped English conjunction)

**Testing:**
- 64 unit + integration tests in `test_enrichment.py`: happy-path strips, homograph protection (11 BLOCK cases), base-language preservation, defensive edges, German noun capitalization, apostrophe non-empty invariant (parametrized over 12 tuples)
- One end-to-end integration test stubs `httpx.AsyncClient`, calls `run_enrichment` with `German`/`English`, asserts both strip and capitalization apply, plus confirms `die alone` homograph survives the full pipeline
- Adjacent suites `test_orchestration_feeder.py` (21) and `test_concept_lyric_levels.py` (33) — no regressions
- Total: 118 passed in 0.95s

**Review history:**
- Pass-1 adversarial review flagged 4 BLOCK-severity homograph bugs plus test coverage gaps
- Pass-2 narrow verification confirmed all BLOCK items closed in code (not just claimed)
- Approved, committed, pushed

**Scope discipline held throughout:** `src/services/events.py` and `tests/test_events_helper.py` remained unstaged and untouched across all three review rounds — unrelated in-flight telemetry work deliberately left out of this commit.

